* ''Train R, block and inline sigils at parsing parity'' (operator approval, 2026-11-01: //"Approve 1 + 2a(3 floor) cleanup of inline vs block sigils to tw5 pono parsing parity"//). A block sigil owns its line, the seal rides the ETX foot as a named value, a sigil whose `>>` leaves text after it reads inline as TiddlyWiki splits it, and trailing text reads as a recovered node with a diagnostic, never silent. Two addons ride it (operator, 2026-11-01): every code fence in the boot seed names its grammar, so the syntax plugin colours it (//"code-fenced blocks in the boot seed should get the grammar marked explicitly"//), and a fence opens and closes with more ticks than the longest run inside it. It follows ''Q'' as its own train and keeps the before-`L4` property. Landed, PR #150 (#/o-takiage).

